.SS cache\-insert
.sp
This command inserts a host into the cache.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.4.0 (host_cache hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see cache\-insert command \%<#\:command-cache-insert>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqcache\-insert\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq01:02:03:04:05:06\(dq,
        \(dqsubnet\-id4\(dq: 4,
        \(dqsubnet\-id6\(dq: 0,
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.100\(dq,
        \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqsomehost.example.org\(dq,
        \(dqclient\-classes4\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqclient\-classes6\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqoption\-data4\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqoption\-data6\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqnext\-server\(dq: \(dq192.0.0.2\(dq,
        \(dqserver\-hostname\(dq: \(dqserver\-hostname.example.org\(dq,
        \(dqboot\-file\-name\(dq: \(dqbootfile.efi\(dq,
        \(dqhost\-id\(dq: 0
    }
}

Another example that adds IPv6 host reservation to cache is:
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqcache\-insert\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq01:02:03:04:05:06\(dq,
        \(dqsubnet\-id4\(dq: 0,
        \(dqsubnet\-id6\(dq: 6,
        \(dqip\-addresses\(dq: [ \(dq2001:db8::cafe:babe\(dq ],
        \(dqprefixes\(dq: [ \(dq2001:db8:dead:beef::/64\(dq ],
        \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
        \(dqclient\-classes4\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqclient\-classes6\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqoption\-data4\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqoption\-data6\(dq: [ ],
        \(dqnext\-server\(dq: \(dq0.0.0.0\(dq,
        \(dqserver\-hostname\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
        \(dqboot\-file\-name\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
        \(dqhost\-id\(dq: 0
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
