.SS cache\-remove
.sp
This command removes entries from the host cache. It takes parameters similar to the \fBreservation\-get\fP command.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.4.0 (host_cache hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see cache\-remove command \%<#\:command-cache-remove>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqcache\-remove\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.1\(dq,
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 123
    }
}

Another example that removes the IPv6 host identifier by DUID and specific subnet\-id is:
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqcache\-remove\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq00:01:ab:cd:f0:a1:c2:d3:e4\(dq,
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 123
    }
}
.EE
