.SS class\-add
.sp
This command adds a new class to the existing server configuration.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.5.0 (class_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see class\-add command \%<#\:command-class-add>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqclass\-add\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqclient\-classes\(dq: [ {
           \(dqname\(dq: <name of the class>,
           \(dqtest\(dq: <test expression to be evaluated on incoming packets>,
           \(dqoption\-data\(dq: [ <option values here> ],
           \(dqoption\-def\(dq: [ <option definitions here> ],
           \(dqnext\-server\(dq: <ipv4 address>,
           \(dqserver\-hostname\(dq: <string>,
           \(dqboot\-file\-name\(dq: <name of the boot file>
        } ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBnext\-server\fP, \fBserver\-hostname\fP, and \fBboot\-file\-name\fP are DHCPv4\-specific. Only one client class can be added with a single command.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqClass \(aq<class\-name>\(aq added.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The command is successful (result 0), unless the class name is a duplicate or another error occurs (result 1).
.SS class\-del
.sp
This command removes a client class from the server configuration.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.5.0 (class_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see class\-del command \%<#\:command-class-del>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqclass\-del\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqname\(dq: <name of the class>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqClass \(aq<class\-name>\(aq deleted.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The command returns a result of 3 (empty) if the client class does not exist. If the client class exists, the returned result is 0 if the deletion was successful; the result is 1 if the deletion is unsuccessful.
.SS class\-get
.sp
This command returns detailed information about an existing client class.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.5.0 (class_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see class\-get command \%<#\:command-class-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqclass\-get\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqname\(dq: <name of the class>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqClass \(aq<class\-name>\(aq definition returned\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqclient\-classes\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqname\(dq: <name of the class>,
                \(dqonly\-in\-additional\-list\(dq: <only in additional list boolean value>,
                \(dqtest\(dq: <test expression to be evaluated on incoming packets>,
                \(dqoption\-data\(dq: [ <option values here> ],
                \(dqoption\-def\(dq: [ <option definitions here> ],
                \(dqnext\-server\(dq: <ipv4 address>,
                \(dqserver\-hostname\(dq: <string>,
                \(dqboot\-file\-name\(dq: <name of the boot file>
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The returned information depends on the DHCP server type, i.e. some parameters are specific to the DHCPv4 server. Also, some parameters may not be returned if they are not set for the client class. If a class with the specified name does not exist, a result of 3 (empty) is returned. If the client class is found, the result of 0 is returned. If there is an error while processing the command, the result of 1 is returned.
.SS class\-list
.sp
This command retrieves a list of all client classes from the server configuration.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.5.0 (class_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see class\-list command \%<#\:command-class-list>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqclass\-list\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This command includes no arguments.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq\(aq<number of>\(aq classes found\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqclient\-classes\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqname\(dq: <first class name>
            },
            {
                \(dqname\(dq: <second class name>
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The returned list of classes merely contains their names.
In order to retrieve full information about one of these
classes, use The class\-get Command \%<#\:command-class-get>\&.
The returned result is 3 (empty) if no classes are found.
If the command is processed successfully and the list of
client classes is not empty, the result of 0 is returned.
If there is an error while processing the command, the
result of 1 is returned.
.SS class\-update
.sp
This command updates an existing client class in the server configuration.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.5.0 (class_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see class\-update command \%<#\:command-class-update>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqclass\-update\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqclient\-classes\(dq: [ {
           \(dqname\(dq: <name of the class>,
           \(dqtest\(dq: <test expression to be evaluated on incoming packets>,
           \(dqoption\-data\(dq: [ <option values here> ],
           \(dqoption\-def\(dq: [ <option definitions here> ],
           \(dqnext\-server\(dq: <ipv4 address>,
           \(dqserver\-hostname\(dq: <string>,
           \(dqboot\-file\-name\(dq: <name of the boot file>
        } ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBnext\-server\fP, \fBserver\-hostname\fP, and \fBboot\-file\-name\fP are DHCPv4\-specific. Only one client class can be updated with a single command.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqClass \(aq<class\-name>\(aq updated.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The command returns the result of 3 (empty) if the client class does not exist. If the client class exists, the returned result is 0 if the update was successful, or 1 if the update is unsuccessful.
.SS config\-backend\-pull
.sp
This command forces an immediate update of the server using Config Backends.
This command does not take any parameters.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.7.1 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see config\-backend\-pull command \%<#\:command-config-backend-pull>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqconfig\-backend\-pull\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqOn demand configuration update successful.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
When no Config Backends are configured this command returns empty (3);
If an error occurs error (1) is returned with the error details;
otherwise success (0) is returned.
.SS config\-get
.sp
This command retrieves the current configuration used by the server. The configuration is essentially the same as the contents of the configuration file, but includes additional changes made by other commands and due to parameters\(aq inheritance.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.2.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see config\-get command \%<#\:command-config-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqconfig\-get\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This command takes no parameters.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        <Dhcp4, Dhcp6, or DhcpDdns object>: <JSON configuration here>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Starting with Kea 2.4.0, the successful response contains an SHA256 digest of the configuration that was
just retrieved. It might be used to determine if a configuration has been modified or not, possibly with the
use of config\-hash\-get.
.SS config\-hash\-get
.sp
This command retrieves the hash of the current configuration used by the server. The
configuration is essentially the same as the contents of the configuration file, but
includes additional changes made by other commands and due to parameters\(aq inheritance.
Currently it is SHA256, but the algorithm may change in the future.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 2.4.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see config\-hash\-get command \%<#\:command-config-hash-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqconfig\-hash\-get\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This command takes no parameters.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqhash\(dq: <SHA256 hash of the config in hexa>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS config\-reload
.sp
This command instructs Kea to reload the configuration file that was used previously.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.2.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see config\-reload command \%<#\:command-config-reload>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqconfig\-reload\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS config\-set
.sp
This command instructs the server to replace its current configuration with the new configuration supplied in the command\(aqs arguments.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.2.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see config\-set command \%<#\:command-config-set>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqconfig\-set\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq:  {
        \(dq\(aq<server>\(aq\(dq: {
        }
     }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In the example below, \(aq<server>\(aq is the configuration element name for a given server such as \(dqDhcp4\(dq or \(dqDhcp6\(dq.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqhash\(dq: \(dq8B5F5822E93178B65CE658304C37EA511BDE7D29F792AA5E88012FC741F2BE32\(dq
    },
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqConfiguration successful.\(dq
}

or

{ \(dqresult\(dq: 1, \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqunsupported parameter: BOGUS (<string>:16:26)\(dq }
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Starting with Kea 2.4.0, the successful response from a DHCPv4, DHCPv6, or DHCP\-DDNS daemons
also contain a SHA\-256 digest of the newly set configuration. The digest can be used to easily
determine if a configuration has been modified or not, possibly with the use of config\-hash\-get.
.SS config\-test
.sp
This command instructs the server to check whether the new configuration supplied in the command\(aqs arguments can be loaded.
