.SS kea\-lfc\-start
.sp
This command starts the kea\-lfc process which cleans up the lease file.
This command does not take any parameters.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 3.1.2 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see kea\-lfc\-start command \%<#\:command-kea-lfc-start>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqkea\-lfc\-start\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
