.UNINDENT
.SS lease4\-add
.sp
This command administratively adds a new IPv4 lease.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease4\-add command \%<#\:command-lease4-add>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-add\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.202\(dq,
        \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq1a:1b:1c:1d:1e:1f\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Note that Kea 1.4 requires an additional argument, subnet\-ID, which is optional as of Kea 1.5. A number of other, more\-detailed, optional arguments are also supported.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the returned result is equal to 4, it indicates that the lease could not be created because it was in conflict with the server\(aqs state or its notion of the configuration. The High Availability hook library can handle such a result differently than a general error. A general error of 1 can indicate issues with processing the command, database availability etc.
.SS lease4\-del
.sp
This command deletes a lease from the lease database.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease4\-del command \%<#\:command-lease4-del>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-del\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.202\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The lease to be deleted can be specified either by IP address or by identifier\-type and identifier value. The currently supported identifiers are \(dqhw\-address\(dq and \(dqclient\-id\(dq.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS lease4\-get
.sp
This command queries the lease database and retrieves existing leases.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease4\-get command \%<#\:command-lease4-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-get\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.1\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqclient\-id\(dq: \(dq42:42:42:42:42:42:42:42\(dq,
    \(dqcltt\(dq: 12345678,
    \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
    \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: true,
    \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqmyhost.example.com.\(dq,
    \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq08:08:08:08:08:08\(dq,
    \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.1\(dq,
    \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
    \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 44,
    \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 3600
  },
  \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
  \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqIPv4 lease found.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
lease4\-get returns a result that indicates the outcome of the operation and lease details,
if found. It has one of the following values: 0 (success), 1 (error), or 3 (empty).
Result 3 is returned if no leases are found with specified IP address.
.SS lease4\-get\-all
.sp
This command retrieves all IPv4 leases or all leases for the specified set of subnets.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.4.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease4\-get\-all command \%<#\:command-lease4-get-all>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-get\-all\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [ 1, 2, 3, ... ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBlease4\-get\-all\fP command may result in very large responses. Please consider using
\fBlease4\-get\-page\fP to get them in chunks. The \fBsubnets\fP parameter is optional. If not
specified, leases from all subnets are returned.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqleases\(dq: [
      {
        \(dqclient\-id\(dq: \(dq01:00:0c:01:02:03:04\(dq,
        \(dqcltt\(dq: 1600432232,
        \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
        \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: false,
        \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
        \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq00:0c:01:02:03:04\(dq,
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.168.1.150\(dq,
        \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 1,
        \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 4000
      },
      {
        \(dqclient\-id\(dq: \(dq01:00:0c:01:02:03:05\(dq,
        \(dqcltt\(dq: 1600432234,
        \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
        \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: false,
        \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
        \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq00:0c:01:02:03:05\(dq,
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.168.1.151\(dq,
        \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 1,
        \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 4000
      }
    ]
  },
  \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
  \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq2 IPv4 lease(s) found.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result 0 is returned when at least one lease is found, 1 when parameters are malformed or missing,
3 is returned if no leases are found with specified parameter.
