Description and examples: see lease4\-resend\-ddns command \%<#\:command-lease4-resend-ddns>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-resend\-ddns\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.1\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
  },
  \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
  \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqNCR generated for: 192.0.2.1, hostname: example.com.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
lease4\-resend\-ddns returns a result that indicates the outcome of the operation and lease details, if found. It has one of the following values: 0 (success), 1 (error), or 3 (empty).
.SS lease4\-update
.sp
This command updates existing leases.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease4\-update command \%<#\:command-lease4-update>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-update\(dq,
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.1\(dq,
    \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqnewhostname.example.org\(dq,
    \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq1a:1b:1c:1d:1e:1f\(dq,
    \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 44,
    \(dqforce\-create\(dq: true
  }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the returned result is equal to 4, it indicates that the lease could not be updated because it was in conflict with the server\(aqs state or its notion of the configuration. The High Availability hook library can handle such a result differently than a general error. A general error of 1 can indicate issues with processing the command, database availability etc.
.SS lease4\-wipe
.sp
This command removes all leases associated with a given subnet.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease4\-wipe command \%<#\:command-lease4-wipe>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-wipe\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 44
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
