.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease4\-write\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqfilename\(dq: \(dqa_file.csv\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS lease6\-add
.sp
This command administratively creates a new lease.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-add command \%<#\:command-lease6-add>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-add\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 66,
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8::3\(dq,
        \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq1a:1b:1c:1d:1e:1f:20:21:22:23:24\(dq,
        \(dqiaid\(dq: 1234
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
lease6\-add can be also used to add leases for IPv6 prefixes.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{ \(dqresult\(dq: 0, \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqLease added.\(dq }
or
{ \(dqresult\(dq: 1, \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqmissing parameter \(aqip\-address\(aq (<string>:3:19)\(dq }
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the returned result is equal to 4, it indicates that the lease could not be created because it was in conflict with the server\(aqs state or its notion of the configuration. The High Availability hook library can handle such a result differently than a general error. A general error of 1 can indicate issues with processing the command, database availability etc.
.SS lease6\-bulk\-apply
.sp
This command creates, updates, or deletes multiple IPv6 leases in a single transaction. It communicates lease changes between HA peers, but may be used in all cases where it is desirable to apply multiple lease updates in a single transaction.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-bulk\-apply command \%<#\:command-lease6-bulk-apply>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-bulk\-apply\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqdeleted\-leases\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:abcd::\(dq,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_PD\(dq,
                ...
            },
            {
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:abcd::234\(dq,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_NA\(dq,
                ...
            }
        ],
        \(dqleases\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 66,
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:cafe::\(dq,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_PD\(dq,
                ...
            },
            {
                \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 66,
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:abcd::333\(dq,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_NA\(dq,
                ...
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If any of the leases is malformed, all changes are rolled back. If the leases are well\-formed but the operation fails for one or more leases, these leases are listed in the response; however, the changes are preserved for all leases for which the operation was successful. The \(dqdeleted\-leases\(dq and \(dqleases\(dq are optional parameters, but one of them must be specified.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqIPv6 leases bulk apply completed.\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqfailed\-deleted\-leases\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:abcd::\(dq,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_PD\(dq,
                \(dqresult\(dq: <control result>,
                \(dqerror\-message\(dq: <error message>
            }
        ],
        \(dqfailed\-leases\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:cafe::\(dq,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_PD\(dq,
                \(dqresult\(dq: <control result>,
                \(dqerror\-message\(dq: <error message>
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \(dqfailed\-deleted\-leases\(dq holds the list of leases which failed to delete; this includes leases which were not found in the database. The \(dqfailed\-leases\(dq includes the list of leases which failed to create or update. For each lease for which there was an error during processing, insertion into the database, etc., the result is set to 1. If an error occurs due to a conflict between the lease and the server\(aqs configuration or state, the result of 4 is returned instead of 1. For each lease which was not deleted because the server did not find it in the database, the result of 3 is returned.
.SS lease6\-del
.sp
This command deletes a lease from the lease database.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
