.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-del\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8::3\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
lease6\-del returns a result that indicates the outcome of the operation. It has one of the following values: 0 (success), 1 (error), or 3 (empty).
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS lease6\-get
.sp
This command queries the lease database and retrieves existing leases.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-get command \%<#\:command-lease6-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-get\(dq,
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1234:ab::\(dq,
    \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_PD\(dq
  }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
lease6\-get returns a result that indicates the outcome of the operation and lease details, if found.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqleases\(dq: [
      {
        \(dqcltt\(dq: 1600439560,
        \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq00:01:00:01:26:f7:81:88:00:0c:01:02:03:04\(dq,
        \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
        \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: false,
        \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqfoobar.example.org\(dq,
        \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq00:0c:01:02:03:04\(dq,
        \(dqiaid\(dq: 1,
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::\(dq,
        \(dqpreferred\-lft\(dq: 3000,
        \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 1,
        \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_NA\(dq,
        \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 4000
      }
    ]
  },
  \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
  \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq1 IPv6 lease(s) found.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result 0 is returned when at least one lease is found, 1 when parameters are malformed or missing,
3 is returned if no leases are found with specified parameter.
.SS lease6\-get\-all
.sp
This command retrieves all IPv6 leases or all leases for the specified set of subnets.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-get\-all command \%<#\:command-lease6-get-all>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-get\-all\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [ 1, 2, 3, 4 ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBlease6\-get\-all\fP command may result in very large responses. Please consider using
\fBlease6\-get\-page\fP to get them in chunks. the \fBsubnets\fP parameter is optional. If not
specified, leases from all subnets are returned.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqleases\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqcltt\(dq: 12345678,
                \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq42:42:42:42:42:42:42:42\(dq,
                \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
                \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: true,
                \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqmyhost.example.com.\(dq,
                \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq08:08:08:08:08:08\(dq,
                \(dqiaid\(dq: 1,
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:2::1\(dq,
                \(dqpreferred\-lft\(dq: 500,
                \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
                \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 44,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_NA\(dq,
                \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 3600
            },
            {
                \(dqcltt\(dq: 12345678,
                \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq21:21:21:21:21:21:21:21\(dq,
                \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
                \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: true,
                \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
                \(dqiaid\(dq: 1,
                \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:0:0:2::\(dq,
                \(dqpreferred\-lft\(dq: 500,
                \(dqprefix\-len\(dq: 80,
                \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
                \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 44,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_PD\(dq,
                \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 3600
            }
        ]
    },
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq2 IPv6 lease(s) found.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result 0 is returned when at least one lease is found, 1 when parameters are malformed or missing,
3 is returned if no leases are found with specified parameter.
