.SS lease6\-get\-page
.sp
This command retrieves all IPv6 leases by page.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.5.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-get\-page command \%<#\:command-lease6-get-page>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-get\-page\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqlimit\(dq: <integer>,
        \(dqfrom\(dq: <IPv6 address or \(aqstart\(aq>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The from address and the page size limit are mandatory.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
  {
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
      \(dqleases\(dq: [
        {
          \(dqcltt\(dq: 1600439560,
          \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq00:01:00:01:26:f7:81:88:00:0c:01:02:03:04\(dq,
          \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
          \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: false,
          \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqfoo.example.org\(dq,
          \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq00:0c:01:02:03:04\(dq,
          \(dqiaid\(dq: 1,
          \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::1\(dq,
          \(dqpreferred\-lft\(dq: 3000,
          \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
          \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 1,
          \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_NA\(dq,
          \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 4000
        },
        {
          \(dqcltt\(dq: 1600439570,
          \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq00:01:00:01:26:f7:81:88:00:0c:01:02:03:05\(dq,
          \(dqfqdn\-fwd\(dq: false,
          \(dqfqdn\-rev\(dq: false,
          \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqbar.example.org\(dq,
          \(dqhw\-address\(dq: \(dq00:0c:01:02:03:05\(dq,
          \(dqiaid\(dq: 1,
          \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::2\(dq,
          \(dqpreferred\-lft\(dq: 3000,
          \(dqstate\(dq: 0,
          \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 1,
          \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqIA_NA\(dq,
          \(dqvalid\-lft\(dq: 4000
        }
      ]
    },
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq1 IPv6 lease(s) found.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result 0 is returned when at least one lease is found, 1 when parameters are malformed or missing,
3 is returned if no leases are found.
.SS lease6\-resend\-ddns
.sp
This command resends a request to kea\-dhcp\-ddns to update DNS for an existing lease.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.7.6 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-resend\-ddns command \%<#\:command-lease6-resend-ddns>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-resend\-ddns\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8::1\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
  },
  \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
  \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqNCR generated for: 2001:db8::1, hostname: example.com.\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
lease6\-resend\-ddns returns a result that indicates the outcome of the operation and lease details, if found. It has one of the following values: 0 (success), 1 (error), or 3 (empty).
.SS lease6\-update
.sp
This command updates existing leases.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see lease6\-update command \%<#\:command-lease6-update>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqlease6\-update\(dq,
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqip\-address\(dq: \(dq2001:db8::1\(dq,
    \(dqduid\(dq: \(dq88:88:88:88:88:88:88:88\(dq,
    \(dqiaid\(dq: 7654321,
    \(dqhostname\(dq: \(dqnewhostname.example.org\(dq,
    \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: 66,
    \(dqforce\-create\(dq: false
  }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the returned result is equal to 4, it indicates that the lease could not be updated because it was in conflict with the server\(aqs state or its notion of the configuration. The High Availability hook library can handle such a result differently than a general error. A general error of 1 can indicate issues with processing the command, database availability etc.
.SS lease6\-wipe
.sp
This command removes all leases associated with a given subnet.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (lease_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
