{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqremote\-option6\-global\-set\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqoptions\(dq: [
            {
                <global option specification>
            }
        ],
        \(dqremote\(dq: {
            <specification of the database to connect to>
        },
        \(dqserver\-tags\(dq: [ <single server tag as string> ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The provided list must contain exactly one option specification. The \fBserver\-tags\fP list is mandatory and must contain exactly one server tag. Specifying an empty list, a value of \fBnull\fP, or multiple server tags will result in an error. The server tag \(dqall\(dq is allowed; it associates the specified option with all servers.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqDHCPv6 option set.\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqoptions\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqcode\(dq: <option code>,
                \(dqspace\(dq: <option space>,
                \(dqclient\-classes\(dq: [ <one or more comma\-separated strings> ]
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
