The server tag is the unique identifier of the server, used to associate the configuration elements in the database with the particular server instance. The returned server description is specified by the user when setting the server information.
.SS remote\-server4\-get\-all
.sp
This command fetches information about all DHCPv4 servers specified by the user.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (cb_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see remote\-server4\-get\-all command \%<#\:command-remote-server4-get-all>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqremote\-server4\-get\-all\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqremote\(dq: {
            <specification of the database to connect to>
        }
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This command contains no arguments besides the optional \fBremote\fP\&.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqDHCPv4 servers found.\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqservers\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqserver\-tag\(dq: <first server tag>,
                \(dqdescription\(dq: <first server description>
            },
            {
                \(dqserver\-tag\(dq: <second server tag>,
                \(dqdescription\(dq: <second server description>
            }
        ],
        \(dqcount\(dq: 2
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The returned response contain a list of maps. Each map contains a server tag uniquely identifying a server, and the user\-defined description of the server. The Kea Configuration Backend uses the keyword \fBall\fP to associate parts of the configuration with all servers. Internally, it creates the logical server \fBall\fP for this purpose. However, this logical server is not returned as a result of the \fBremote\-server4\-get\-all\fP command; only the user\-defined servers are returned.
.SS remote\-server4\-set
.sp
This command creates or replaces information about the DHCPv4 server in the database.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (cb_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see remote\-server4\-set command \%<#\:command-remote-server4-set>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqremote\-server4\-set\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqservers\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqserver\-tag\(dq: <server tag>,
                \(dqdescription\(dq: <server description>
            }
        ],
        \(dqremote\(dq: {
            <specification of the database to connect to>
        }
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The provided list must contain exactly one server specification. The \fBserver\-tag\fP must be unique across all servers within the configuration database. The \fBdescription\fP is the arbitrary text describing the server, its location within the network, etc.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqDHCPv4 server successfully set.\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqservers\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqserver\-tag\(dq: <server tag>,
                \(dqdescription\(dq: <server description>
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS remote\-server6\-del
.sp
This command deletes information about a DHCPv6 server from the configuration database. Any configuration explicitly associated with the deleted server is automatically disassociated. In addition, configuration elements not shareable with other servers (e.g. global DHCP parameters) are deleted. Shareable configuration elements (e.g. subnets, shared networks) are not deleted as they may be used by other servers.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (cb_cmds hook library)
