.SS remote\-subnet4\-list
.sp
This command fetches a list of all IPv4 subnets from the configuration database.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (cb_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see remote\-subnet4\-list command \%<#\:command-remote-subnet4-list>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqremote\-subnet4\-list\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqremote\(dq: {
            <specification of the database to connect to>
        },
        \(dqserver\-tags\(dq: [ <first server tag>, <second server tag>, ... ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBserver\-tags\fP list is required for this command, and must not be empty. It may either contain one or multiple server tags as strings, or a single \fBnull\fP value.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq2 IPv4 subnets found.\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: <first subnet identifier>,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: <first subnet prefix>,
                \(dqshared\-network\-name\(dq: <shared network name or null>,
                \(dqmetadata\(dq: {
                    \(dqserver\-tags\(dq: [ <first server tag>, <second server tag>, ... ]
                }
            },
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: <second subnet identifier>,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: <second subnet prefix>,
                \(dqshared\-network\-name\(dq: <shared network name or null>,
                \(dqmetadata\(dq: {
                    \(dqserver\-tags\(dq: [ <first server tag>, ... ]
                }
            }
        ],
        \(dqcount\(dq: 2
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The returned response contains a list of maps. Each map contains a subnet identifier, prefix, and shared network name to which the subnet belongs. If the subnet does not belong to a shared network, the name is null. The metadata includes database\-specific information associated with the subnets. The returned list does not contain full subnet definitions; use \fBremote\-subnet4\-get\fP to fetch the full information about the selected subnets. If the command includes explicit server tags as strings (including the special server tag \(dqall\(dq), the list contains all subnets which are associated with any of the specified tags. A subnet is returned even if it is associated with multiple servers and only one of the specified tags matches. If the command includes the \fBnull\fP value in the \fBserver\-tags\fP list, the response contains all subnets which are assigned to no servers (unassigned).
.SS remote\-subnet4\-set
.sp
This command creates or replaces an IPv4 subnet in the configuration database.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (cb_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see remote\-subnet4\-set command \%<#\:command-remote-subnet4-set>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqremote\-subnet4\-set\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: <subnet identifier>,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: <subnet prefix>,
                \(dqshared\-network\-name\(dq: <shared network name or null>,
                <the rest of the subnet specification here>
            }
        ],
        \(dqremote\(dq: {
            <specification of the database to connect to>
        },
        \(dqserver\-tags\(dq: [ <first server tag>, <second server tag>, ... ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The provided list must contain exactly one subnet specification. The \fBshared\-network\-name\fP parameter is required for these commands; it associates the subnet with the shared network by its name. If the subnet must not belong to any shared network (a global subnet), the \fBnull\fP value must be specified for the shared network name. The \fBserver\-tags\fP list is mandatory and must contain one or more server tags as strings to explicitly associate the subnet with one or more user\-defined servers. The \fBremote\-subnet4\-set\fP command may include the special server tag \(dqall\(dq to associate the subnet with all servers.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqIPv4 subnet successfully set.\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqid\(dq: <subnet identifier>,
        \(dqsubnet\(dq: <subnet prefix>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
