.UNINDENT
.sp
The reservation\-get\-all command may result in very large responses.
.SS reservation\-get\-by\-address
.sp
This command retrieves all host reservations for given ip\-address and optionally a specified subnet.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 2.4.0 (host_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see reservation\-get\-by\-address command \%<#\:command-reservation-get-by-address>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqreservation\-get\-by\-address\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqip\-address\(dq: <string>,
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: <integer>,
        \(dqoperation\-target\(dq: <string (memory, database, all, default)>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The host reservations can be identified by a pair of \(aqip\-address\(aq and \(aqsubnet\-id\(aq. \(aqsubnet\-id\(aq is optional. \(aqoperation\-target\(aq is optional; default is \(aqall\(aq.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
