.SS reservation\-get\-page
.sp
This command retrieves all host reservations or host reservations for a specified subnet by page.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (host_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see reservation\-get\-page command \%<#\:command-reservation-get-page>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqreservation\-get\-page\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: <integer>,
        \(dqlimit\(dq: <integer>,
        \(dqsource\-index\(dq: <integer>,
        \(dqfrom\(dq: <integer>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The page size limit is mandatory. The subnet\-id is optional since version 1.9.0. The source\-index and from host\-id are optional and default to 0. Values to use to load the next page are returned in responses in a next map.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS reservation\-update
.sp
This command updates an existing host reservation. The reservation has to include host identifiers and a subnet identifier and may include IPv4 addresses, IPv6 addresses, IPv6 prefixes, various identifiers, a class the client will be assigned to, DHCPv4 and DHCPv6 options, and more.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 2.3.7 (host_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see reservation\-update command \%<#\:command-reservation-update>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqreservation\-update\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqreservation\(dq: {
            \(dqboot\-file\-name\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqclient\-id\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqcircuit\-id\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqduid\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqflex\-id\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqip\-address\(dq: <string (IPv4 address)>,
            \(dqip\-addresses\(dq: [ <comma\-separated strings> ],
            \(dqhw\-address\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqhostname\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqnext\-server\(dq: <string (IPv4 address)>,
            \(dqoption\-data\(dq: [ <comma\-separated structures defining options> ],
            \(dqprefixes\(dq: [ <comma\-separated IPv6 prefixes> ],
            \(dqclient\-classes\(dq: [ <comma\-separated strings> ],
            \(dqserver\-hostname\(dq: <string>,
            \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq: <integer>,
            \(dquser\-context\(dq: <any valid JSON>
        },
        \(dqoperation\-target\(dq: <string (memory, database, all, default)>
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Note that boot\-file\-name, circuit\-id, client\-id, ip\-address, next\-server, and server\-hostname are IPv4\-specific. ip\-addresses, and prefixes are IPv6\-specific. Operation\-target is optional; default is \(aqalternate\(aq.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: <string>
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS server\-tag\-get
.sp
This command returns the server tag used by the server.
Server tag is essential configuration parameter in the Config Backend configuration.
This parameter is configured in the local config file.
This command does not take any parameters.
