    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
      \(dqresult\-set\(dq: {
        \(dqcolumns\(dq: [ \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq, \(dqtotal\-addresses\(dq, \(dqcumulative\-assigned\-addresses\(dq, \(dqassigned\-addresses\(dq, \(dqdeclined\-addresses\(dq ],
        \(dqrows\(dq: [
          [ 10, 256, 200, 111, 0 ],
          [ 20, 4098, 5000, 2034, 4 ]
        ],
        \(dqtimestamp\(dq: \(dq2018\-05\-04 15:03:37.000000\(dq
      }
    }
  }
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS stat\-lease6\-get
.sp
This command fetches lease statistics for a range of known IPv6 subnets.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.4.0 (stat_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see stat\-lease6\-get command \%<#\:command-stat-lease6-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
  \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqstat\-lease6\-get\(dq,
  \(dqarguments\(dq: {
    \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq : 10
  }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqstat\-lease6\-get: 2 rows found\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
      \(dqresult\-set\(dq: {
        \(dqcolumns\(dq: [ \(dqsubnet\-id\(dq, \(dqtotal\-nas\(dq, \(dqcumulative\-assigned\-nas\(dq, \(dqassigned\-nas\(dq, \(dqdeclined\-addresses\(dq, \(dqtotal\-pds\(dq, \(dqcumulative\-assigned\-pds\(dq, \(dqassigned\-pds\(dq ],
        \(dqrows\(dq: [
          [ 10, 4096, 3000, 2400, 3, 0, 0],
          [ 20, 0, 0, 0, 1048, 500, 233 ],
          [ 30, 256, 300, 60, 0, 1048, 15, 15 ]
        ],
        \(dqtimestamp\(dq: \(dq2018\-05\-04 15:03:37.000000\(dq
      }
    }
  }
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS statistic\-get
.sp
This command retrieves a single statistic. It takes a single string parameter called name that specifies the statistic name.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.0.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see statistic\-get command \%<#\:command-statistic-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqstatistic\-get\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqname\(dq: \(dqpkt4\-received\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The server responds with the details of the requested statistic, with a result of 0 indicating success, and the specified statistic as the value of the \(dqarguments\(dq parameter.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
   \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
   \(dqarguments\(dq: {
       \(dqpkt4\-received\(dq: [ [ \(dqfirst_value\(dq, \(dq2019\-07\-30 10:11:19.498739\(dq ], [ \(dqsecond_value\(dq, \(dq2019\-07\-30 10:11:19.498662\(dq ] ]
       }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS statistic\-get\-all
.sp
This command retrieves all recorded statistics.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.0.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see statistic\-get\-all command \%<#\:command-statistic-get-all>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqstatistic\-get\-all\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: { }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The server responds with the details of all recorded statistics.
