.SS subnet4\-list
.sp
This command lists all currently configured subnets. The subnets are returned in a brief format, i.e. a subnet identifier, subnet prefix, and shared network name (if available) are included for each subnet.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp4
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (subnet_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see subnet4\-list command \%<#\:command-subnet4-list>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqsubnet4\-list\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq2 IPv4 subnets found\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: 10,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq10.0.0.0/8\(dq
            },
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: 100,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq192.0.2.0/24\(dq,
                \(dqshared\-network\-name\(dq: \(dqexample\-shared\-network\(dq
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If no IPv4 subnets are found, an error code is returned along with the error description.
.SS subnet4\-select\-test
