    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqInfo about IPv6 subnet 2001:db8:1::/64 (id 11) returned\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::/64\(dq,
                \(dqid\(dq: 1,
                \(dqoption\-data\(dq: [{
                    ...
                }],
                ...
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS subnet6\-list
.sp
This command lists all currently configured subnets. The subnets are returned in a brief format, i.e. a subnet identifier, subnet prefix, and shared network name are included for each subnet.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.3.0 (subnet_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see subnet6\-list command \%<#\:command-subnet6-list>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqsubnet6\-list\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq2 IPv6 subnets found\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: 11,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::/64\(dq
            },
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: 233,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq3000::/16\(dq,
                \(dqshared\-network\-name\(dq: \(dqexample\-shared\-network\(dq
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If no IPv6 subnets are found, an error code is returned along with the error description.
.SS subnet6\-select\-test
.sp
This command returns the result of DHCPv6 subnet selection
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 2.7.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see subnet6\-select\-test command \%<#\:command-subnet6-select-test>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqsubnet6\-select\-test\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqinterface\(dq: <string>,
        \(dqinterface\-id\(dq: <string>,
        \(dqremote\(dq: <string>,
        \(dqlink\(dq: <string>,
        \(dqclasses\(dq: [ <strings> ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible parameters are the incoming interface name, remote address, relay link address, client classes, etc.
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{ \(dqresult\(dq: 1, \(dqtext\(dq: <localization result> }
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
3 forms for selected shared network, subnet or nothing..
.SS subnet6\-update
.sp
This command updates (overwrites) a single subnet in the existing server configuration. This operation has no impact on other subnets.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.6.0 (subnet_cmds hook library)
.sp
Access: write \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see subnet6\-update command \%<#\:command-subnet6-update>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqsubnet6\-update\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnet6\(dq: [ {
            \(dqid\(dq: 234,
            \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::/64\(dq,
            ...
        } ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: 0,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dqIPv6 subnet updated\(dq,
    \(dqarguments\(dq: {
        \(dqsubnets\(dq: [
            {
                \(dqid\(dq: 234,
                \(dqsubnet\(dq: \(dq2001:db8:1::/64\(dq
            }
        ]
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SS version\-get
.sp
This command returns extended information about the Kea version that is running. The returned string is the same as if Kea were run with the \fB\-V\fP command\-line option.
.sp
Supported by: kea\-dhcp\-ddns, kea\-dhcp4, kea\-dhcp6
.sp
Availability: 1.2.0 (built\-in)
.sp
Access: read \fI(parameter ignored in this Kea version)\fP
.sp
Description and examples: see version\-get command \%<#\:command-version-get>
.sp
Command syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqversion\-get\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Response syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqresult\(dq: <integer>,
    \(dqtext\(dq: \(dq<string>\(dq
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result is an integer representation of the status. Currently supported statuses are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
0 \- success
.IP \(bu 2
1 \- error
.IP \(bu 2
2 \- unsupported
.IP \(bu 2
3 \- empty (command was completed successfully, but no data was affected or returned)
.IP \(bu 2
4 \- conflict (command could not apply requested configuration changes because they were in conflict with the server state)
.UNINDENT
.SH MANUAL PAGES
.SS \fBkea\-dhcp4\fP \- DHCPv4 server in Kea
.SS Synopsis
.sp
\fBkea\-dhcp4\fP [\fB\-v\fP] [\fB\-V\fP] [\fB\-W\fP] [\fB\-d\fP] [\fB\-c\fP config\-file] [\fB\-t\fP config\-file] [\fB\-p\fP server\-port\-number] [\fB\-P\fP client\-port\-number]
.SS Description
.sp
The \fBkea\-dhcp4\fP daemon provides the DHCPv4 server implementation.
.SS Arguments
.sp
The arguments are as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB\-v\fP
Displays the Kea version.
.TP
.B \fB\-V\fP
Displays the extended Kea version.
.TP
.B \fB\-W\fP
Displays the configuration report.
.TP
.B \fB\-d\fP
Enables the debug mode with extra verbosity.
.TP
.B \fB\-c config\-file\fP
Specifies the configuration file with the configuration for the DHCPv4 server. It
may also contain configuration entries for other Kea services.
.TP
.B \fB\-t config\-file\fP
Checks the configuration file and reports the first error, if any. Note
that not all parameters are completely checked; in particular,
service and control channel sockets are not opened, and hook
libraries are not loaded.
.TP
.B \fB\-T config\-file\fP
Checks the configuration file and reports the first error, if any.
It performs extra checks beyond what \-t offers, such as establishing
database connections (for the lease backend, host reservations backend,
configuration backend, and forensic logging backend), loading hook libraries,
parsing hook\-library configurations, etc. It does not open UNIX or TCP/UDP sockets,
nor does it open or rotate files, as any of these actions could interfere
with a running process on the same machine.
.TP
.B \fB\-p server\-port\-number\fP
Specifies the server port number (1\-65535) on which the server listens. This is
useful for testing purposes only.
.TP
.B \fB\-P client\-port\-number\fP
Specifies the client port number (1\-65535) to which the server responds. This is
useful for testing purposes only.
.UNINDENT
.SS Documentation
.sp
Kea comes with an extensive Kea Administrator Reference Manual that covers
all aspects of running the Kea software \- compilation, installation,
configuration, configuration examples, and much more. Kea also features a
Kea Messages Manual, which lists all possible messages Kea can print
with a brief description for each of them. Both documents are
available in various formats (.txt, .html, .pdf) with the Kea
distribution. The Kea documentation is available at
\%<https://\:kea\:.readthedocs\:.io>\&.
.sp
Kea source code is documented in the Kea Developer\(aqs Guide,
available at \%<https://\:reports\:.kea\:.isc\:.org/\:dev_guide>\&.
.sp
The Kea project website is available at \%<https://\:kea\:.isc\:.org>\&.
.SS Mailing Lists and Support
.sp
There are two public mailing lists available for the Kea project. \fBkea\-users\fP
(kea\-users at lists.isc.org) is intended for Kea users, while \fBkea\-dev\fP
(kea\-dev at lists.isc.org) is intended for Kea developers, prospective
contributors, and other advanced users. Both lists are available at
\%<https://\:lists\:.isc\:.org>\&. The community provides best\-effort support
on both of those lists.
.sp
ISC provides professional support for Kea services. See
\%<https://\:www\:.isc\:.org/\:kea> for details.
.SS History
.sp
The \fBb10\-dhcp4\fP daemon was first coded in November 2011 by Tomek
Mrugalski.
.sp
In mid\-2014, Kea was decoupled from the BIND 10 framework and became a
standalone DHCP server. The DHCPv4 server binary was renamed to
\fBkea\-dhcp4\fP\&. Kea 1.0.0 was released in December 2015.
.SS See Also
.sp
\fBkea\-dhcp6(8)\fP, \fBkea\-dhcp\-ddns(8)\fP,
\fBkea\-admin(8)\fP, \fBkeactrl(8)\fP,
\fBperfdhcp(8)\fP, \fBkea\-netconf(8)\fP, \fBkea\-lfc(8)\fP,
Kea Administrator Reference Manual.
