This informational message indicates that the Host Commands hooks library has
been unloaded successfully.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_INIT_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
loading Subnet Commands hooks library failed: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message indicates an error during loading the Subnet Commands
hooks library. The details of the error are provided as argument of
the log message.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_INIT_OK
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
loading Subnet Commands hooks library successful
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message indicates that the Host Commands hooks library has
been loaded successfully. Enjoy!
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK4_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to add new IPv4 network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to add a new IPv4 network to the server configuration. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK4_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to delete IPv4 network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to delete an IPv4 network. The reason for failure is provided within the
error message. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK4_GET_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return an IPv4 network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the server fails to return an IPv4
network in response to \(aqnetwork4\-get\(aq command. The argument details the
reason for failure. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code. This error may occur when the received
command has invalid structure, has not allowed parameters or lacks required
parameters. It will also be returned when the command syntax is correct
but no network was found.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK4_LIST_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return a list of IPv4 networks: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to return a list of IPv4 networks requested with \(aqnetwork4\-list\(aq command. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message
will be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK4_SUBNET_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to add existing IPv4 subnet to a shared network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to add existing IPv4 subnet to existing shared network. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK4_SUBNET_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to remove a IPv4 subnet from a shared network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to remove existing IPv4 subnet to existing shared network. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK6_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to add new IPv6 network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to add a new IPv6 network to the server configuration. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK6_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to delete IPv6 network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to delete an IPv6 network. The reason for failure is provided within the
error message. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK6_GET_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return an IPv6 network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the server fails to return an IPv6
network in response to \(aqnetwork4\-get\(aq command. The argument details the
reason for failure. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code. This error may occur when the received
command has invalid structure, has not allowed parameters or lacks required
parameters. It will also be returned when the command syntax is correct
but no network was found.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK6_LIST_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return a list of IPv6 networks: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to return a list of IPv4 networks requested with \(aqnetwork6\-list\(aq command. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message
will be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK6_SUBNET_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to add existing IPv6 subnet to a shared network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to add existing IPv6 subnet to existing shared network. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK6_SUBNET_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to remove a IPv6 subnet from a shared network: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to remove existing IPv6 subnet to existing shared network. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_ADD
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully added shared network %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully adds a shared network as a result of receiving a \(aqnetwork4\-add\(aq
or \(aqnetwork6\-add\(aq command\(aq. The argument represents the name of added shared
network.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_DEL
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully deleted shared network %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully deletes a shared network as a result of receiving a \(aqnetwork4\-del\(aq
or \(aqnetwork6\-del\(aq command\(aq. The argument represents the name of deleted shared
network.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_GET
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully retrieved shared network %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully retrieves a shared network as a result of receiving a \(aqnetwork4\-get\(aq
or \(aqnetwork6\-get\(aq command\(aq. The argument represents the name of retrieved shared
network.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_GET_EMPTY
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
specified shared network is not found: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
found no matching shared network as a result of receiving a \(aqnetwork4\-get\(aq or
\(aqnetwork6\-get\(aq command\(aq.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_LIST
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully retrieved list of %1 %2 shared networks
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully retrieves a list of shared networks as a result of receiving \(aqnetwork4\-list\(aq
or \(aqnetwork6\-list\(aq command. The first argument specifies a number of networks
retrieved. The second parameter specifies a protocol type: \(aqIPv4\(aq or \(aqIPv6\(aq.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_LIST_EMPTY
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
no %1 shared networks listed
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully processes the \(aqnetwork4\-list\(aq or \(aqnetwork6\-list\(aq command but
no shared network has been found. This indicates that the server configuration
contains no shared networks of the specific type. The argument specifies a protocol
type: \(aqIPv4\(aq or \(aqIPv6\(aq.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_SUBNET_ADD
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
%1 subnet %2 (id %3) added to shared network %4
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message indicates that specified subnet (address family
given in parameter 1, details in parameters 2 and 3) is now part of a shared
network. This is a successful result of either network4\-subnet\-add or
network6\-subnet\-add commands.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_NETWORK_SUBNET_DEL
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
%1 subnet %2 (id %3) removed from shared network %4
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message indicates that specified subnets (address family
given in parameter 1, details in parameters 2 and 3) is no longer part of a shared
network. The subnet remains in configuration, but is a stand alone subnet.
This is a successful result of either network4\-subnet\-del or network6\-subnet\-del commands.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to add new IPv4 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to add a new IPv4 subnet to the server configuration. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_DELTA_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to update IPv4 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to update by adding a delta in a IPv4 subnet to the server configuration. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message will
be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_DELTA_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to update IPv4 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to update by removing a delta in a IPv4 subnet to the server configuration. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message will
be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to delete IPv4 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to delete an IPv4 subnet. The reason for failure is provided within the
error message. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_GET_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return an IPv4 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the server fails to return an IPv4
subnet in response to \(aqsubnet4\-get\(aq command. The argument details the
reason for failure. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code. This error may occur when the received
command has invalid structure, has not allowed parameters or lacks required
parameters. It will also be returned when the command syntax is correct
but no subnet was found.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_LIST_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return a list of IPv4 subnets: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to return a list of IPv4 subnets requested with \(aqsubnet4\-list\(aq command. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message
will be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET4_UPDATE_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to update IPv4 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to update a IPv4 subnet to the server configuration. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to add new IPv6 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to add a new IPv6 subnet to the server configuration. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_DELTA_ADD_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to update IPv6 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to update by adding a delta in a IPv6 subnet to the server configuration. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message will
be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_DELTA_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to update IPv6 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to update by removing a delta in a IPv6 subnet to the server configuration. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message will
be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_DEL_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to delete IPv6 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to delete an IPv6 subnet. The reason for failure is provided within the
error message. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_GET_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return an IPv6 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the server fails to return an IPv6
subnet in response to \(aqsubnet4\-get\(aq command. The argument details the
reason for failure. The error message will be returned to the controlling
client with the error status code. This error may occur when the received
command has invalid structure, has not allowed parameters or lacks required
parameters. It will also be returned when the command syntax is correct
but no subnet was found.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_LIST_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to return a list of IPv6 subnets: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to return a list of IPv6 subnets requested with \(aqsubnet6\-list\(aq command. The
reason for failure is provided within the error message. The error message
will be returned to the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET6_UPDATE_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
failed to update IPv6 subnet: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library fails
to update a IPv6 subnet to the server configuration. The reason for failure
is provided within the error message. The error message will be returned to
the controlling client with the error status code.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_ADD
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully added subnet %1 having id %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully adds a subnet as a result of receiving a \(aqsubnet4\-add\(aq
or \(aqsubnet6\-add\(aq command\(aq. The first parameter specifies an added subnet
prefix. The second parameter specifies a subnet identifier.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_DEL
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully deleted subnet %1 having id %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully deletes a subnet as a result of receiving a \(aqsubnet4\-del\(aq
or \(aqsubnet6\-del\(aq command\(aq. The first parameter specifies a deleted subnet
prefix. The second parameter specifies a subnet identifier.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_GET
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully retrieved subnet %1 having id %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully retrieves a subnet as a result of receiving a \(aqsubnet4\-get\(aq
or \(aqsubnet6\-get\(aq command\(aq. The first parameter specifies a retrieved subnet
prefix. The second parameter specifies a subnet identifier.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_GET_EMPTY
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
specified subnet is not found: %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
found no a matching subnet as a result of receiving a \(aqsubnet4\-get\(aq or
\(aqsubnet6\-get\(aq command\(aq.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_LIST
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully retrieved list of %1 %2 subnets
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully retrieves a list of subnets as a result of receiving \(aqsubnet4\-list\(aq
or \(aqsubnet6\-list\(aq command. The first argument specifies a number of subnets
retrieved. The second parameter specifies a protocol type: \(aqIPv4\(aq or \(aqIPv6\(aq.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_LIST_EMPTY
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
no %1 subnets listed
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully processes the \(aqsubnet4\-list\(aq or \(aqsubnet6\-list\(aq command but
no subnets have been found. This indicates that the server configuration
contains no subnets of the specific type. This is not an error condition
but it is unusual case for the DHCP service. The argument specifies a type
of the subnets being listed, i.e. \(aqIPv4\(aq or \(aqIPv6\(aq.
.SS SUBNET_CMDS_SUBNET_UPDATE
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
successfully updated subnet %1 having id %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This informational message is issued when the Subnet Commands hooks library
successfully updates a subnet as a result of receiving a \(aqsubnet4\-update\(aq
or \(aqsubnet6\-update\(aq command\(aq. The first parameter specifies an updated subnet
prefix. The second parameter specifies a subnet identifier.
.SS TCP
.SS TCP_CLIENT_BAD_SERVER_RESPONSE_RECEIVED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
bad response received when communicating with %1 port %2: %3
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when a TCP client fails to receive a response
from the server or when this response is malformed. The first arguments
specify the server address and port. The last provides a detailed error
message.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_BAD_SERVER_RESPONSE_RECEIVED_DETAILS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
detailed information about bad response received from %1 port %2:\en%3
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 45.
This debug message is issued when a TCP client receives malformed response
from the server. The first arguments specify the address and port of the
server, The last argument provides a dump of the response.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_CONNECTION_CLOSE_CALLBACK_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
Connection close callback threw an exception
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This is an error message emitted when the close connection callback
registered on the connection failed unexpectedly.  This is a programmatic
error that should be submitted as a bug.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_MT_STARTED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
TcpClient has been started in multi\-threaded mode running %1 threads
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when a multi\-threaded TCP client instance has
been created. The argument specifies the maximum number of threads.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_PREMATURE_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_OCCURRED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
premature connection timeout occurred: in transaction ? %1, transid: %2, current_transid: %3
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This warning message is issued when unexpected timeout occurred during the
transaction. This is proven to occur when the system clock is moved manually
or as a result of synchronization with a time server. Any ongoing transactions
will be interrupted. New transactions should be conducted normally.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_QUEUE_SIZE_GROWING
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
queue for address: %1, port %2, now has %3 entries and may be growing too quickly
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This warning message is issued when the queue of pending requests for the
given address and port appears to be growing more quickly than the requests
can be handled. It will be emitted periodically as long as the queue size
continues to grow. This may occur with a surge of client traffic creating
a momentary backlog which then subsides as the surge subsides. If it happens
continually then it most likely indicates a deployment configuration that
cannot sustain the client load.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_REQUEST_SEND
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
sending TCP request %1 to %2 port %3
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 50.
This debug message is issued when the client is starting to send a TCP
request to a server. The first argument dumps the request, next arguments
specify address and port of the server.
.SS TCP_CLIENT_SERVER_RESPONSE_RECEIVED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
received TCP response from %1 port %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when the client finished receiving a TCP
response from the server. The address and port of the server are specified
as arguments.
.SS TCP_CONNECTION_REJECTED_BY_FILTER
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
connection from %1 has been denied by the connection filter.
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 50.
This debug message is issued when the server\(aqs connection filter rejects
a new connection based on the client\(aqs ip address.
.SS TCP_CONNECTION_SHUTDOWN
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
shutting down TCP connection from %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when one of the TCP connections is shut down.
The connection can be stopped as a result of an error or after the
successful message exchange with a client.
.SS TCP_CONNECTION_SHUTDOWN_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
shutting down TCP connection failed
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when an error occurred during shutting down
a TCP connection with a client.
.SS TCP_CONNECTION_STOP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
stopping TCP connection from %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when one of the TCP connections is stopped.
The connection can be stopped as a result of an error or after the
successful message exchange with a client.
.SS TCP_CONNECTION_STOP_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
stopping TCP connection failed
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when an error occurred during closing a
TCP connection with a client.
.SS TCP_DATA_RECEIVED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
received %1 bytes from %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 55.
This debug message is issued when the server receives a chunk of data from
the remote endpoint. This may include the whole request or only a part
of the request. The first argument specifies the amount of received data.
The second argument specifies an address of the remote endpoint which
produced the data.
.SS TCP_DATA_SENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
send %1 bytes to %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 55.
This debug message is issued when the server sends a chunk of data to
the remote endpoint. This may include the whole response or only a part
of the response. The first argument specifies the amount of sent data.
The second argument specifies an address of the remote endpoint.
.SS TCP_IDLE_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_OCCURRED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
closing connection with %1 as a result of a timeout
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 50.
This debug message is issued when the TCP connection is being closed as a
result of being idle.
.SS TCP_REQUEST_RECEIVED_FAILED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
An unexpected error occurred processing a request from %1, error: %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This error message is issued when an unexpected error occurred while the
server attempted to process a received request. The first argument specifies
the address of the remote endpoint. The second argument describes the nature
error.
.SS TCP_REQUEST_RECEIVE_START
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
start receiving request from %1 with timeout %2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 50.
This debug message is issued when the server starts receiving new request
over the established connection. The first argument specifies the address
of the remote endpoint. The second argument specifies request timeout in
seconds.
.SS TCP_SERVER_CLIENT_REQUEST_RECEIVED
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
received TCP request from %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when the server finished receiving a TCP
request from the remote endpoint. The address of the remote endpoint is
specified as an argument.
.SS TCP_SERVER_RESPONSE_SEND
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
sending TCP response to %1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Logged at debug log level 40.
This debug message is issued when the server is starting to send a TCP
response to a remote endpoint. The argument specifies an address of
the remote endpoint.
